:07:08Z","updated_at":"2026-06-18T14:51:43Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible since Godot 4.6 (Steam)\n- Not present in Godot 4.5 (Steam)\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - Godot 4.6 Steam ver\n\n### Issue description\n\nEver since Godot 4.6, opening the engine from the executable no longer counts playtime on Steam.\nIn Godot 4.5, I was able to pin the project manager to the taskbar and open it from there which would count my hours on Steam without having to start it manually from Steam.\n\nI know this is a small issue but it getting fixed would be very helpful and would save some time for people who care about that.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Pin the Godot project manager to your taskbar\n2. Close it \n3. Start it from the taskbar\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNot necessary","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119049/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119049/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}